ervices, no unwanted socket exposure, healthy package state, and only expected reboot-related temporary-file/PID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-68f9ad7f8f704cdc","cmd-a7e51d859510494c","cmd-e82aa323253a455f","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 demonstrably rebooted from boot ID 6ab6a71b-188c-48ae-971b-a6bb378b1d72 to a57b9526-59ef-4b0b-9e75-7a592fb44ae3, returned with audit=1 active and persistent, and retained its RHEL release and installed kernel. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledged restart, observed interruption, changed boot identity, and recovered services, access, protected-data checksums, and failed-unit state were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":[]}
